  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "What the stage means",
      "items": [
        "A kept link advances only when capture succeeds; the worker skips links that are not kept or active. A blank extraction is flagged.",
        "Plan extraction requires price tables and valid plans. Publication is a separate operator action and publishes only complete, unignored records.",
        "pipeline_stage records business progress; pipeline_task_state separately tracks task execution. NoPlanRecordsError completes with last_error; other exceptions set failed and notify the operator.",
        "Budget exhaustion parks a link while labeling/classification/schema extraction is in progress. Rerun restores the relevant processing stage."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Scope and branches",
      "items": [
        "This lifecycle follows automated per-Link processing from discovery through publication. Manual API calls can invoke capture, extraction, classification, labeling, plan retrieval, and publishing separately.",
        "DEAD_LETTERED is an available model value but this normal worker path does not assign it; it is not shown as a normal transition.",
        "Operator rerun clears the recorded error and resumes from the persisted stage. Dead-lettered links restart at captured if a current trace exists, otherwise discovered."
      ]
    }
  ]
